cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Cloud-Native Architectures and Modern Data Formats for Geoscience"
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the metadata from this file when referring to
  or reusing this training material.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Tobias
    family-names: Ferreira
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0888-9751"
    affiliation: "National Oceanography Centre"
abstract: >-
  A Carpentries-style training lesson on cloud-native architectures and modern
  data formats for geoscience, covering workflows for oceanography, climate,
  and meteorology data at multi-terabyte scale. Topics include Zarr,
  chunking, object storage, conversion from traditional formats,
  parallel processing, Icechunk, VirtualiZarr, STAC, and visualization.
license: CC-BY-NC 4.0
